def render_math_methodology_view():
    render_view_header("MATH_METHODOLOGY")
    st.markdown("<div style='font-family: Playfair Display, serif; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: #3E2723; margin: 10px 0 8px 0;'>📐 Mathematical Formulations & Statistical Methods</div>", unsafe_allow_html=True)
    st.markdown("""
    This section documents the formal mathematical and statistical formulas implemented in the **BananaScope PH Analytics Engine**:

    ### 1. Year-over-Year (YoY) Growth Rate
    $$\\Delta V_t = V_t - V_{t-1}, \\quad \\text{YoY Growth } (\\%) = \\left( \\frac{V_t - V_{t-1}}{V_{t-1}} \\right) \\times 100$$

    ### 2. Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR)
    $$\\text{CAGR} = \\left( \\frac{V_{\\text{end}}}{V_{\\text{start}}} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{n}} - 1$$

    ### 3. Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) Linear Trend
    $$\\hat{y}_t = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 t, \\quad \\beta_1 = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^n (t_i - \\bar{t})(y_i - \\bar{y})}{\\sum_{i=1}^n (t_i - \\bar{t})^2}, \\quad R^2 = 1 - \\frac{\\sum (y_i - \\hat{y}_i)^2}{\\sum (y_i - \\bar{y})^2}$$

    ### 4. Statistical Anomaly & Outlier Detection (Z-Score)
    $$Z_t = \\frac{V_t - \\mu}{\\sigma} \\quad (\\text{Boom: } Z_t > +1.4, \\; \\text{Shock: } Z_t < -1.4)$$

    ### 5. Double Exponential Smoothing (Holt's Linear Forecast)
    $$\\ell_t = \\alpha y_t + (1 - \\alpha)(\\ell_{t-1} + b_{t-1}), \\quad b_t = \\beta (\\ell_t - \\ell_{t-1}) + (1 - \\beta) b_{t-1}, \\quad \\hat{y}_{t+h} = \\ell_t + h b_t$$
    *Parameters:* Smoothing weight $\\alpha = 0.6$, Trend weight $\\beta = 0.2$.

    ### 6. Forecast Accuracy Metrics
    $$\\text{MAE} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum |y_i - \\hat{y}_i|, \\quad \\text{RMSE} = \\sqrt{ \\frac{1}{n} \\sum (y_i - \\hat{y}_i)^2 }, \\quad \\text{MAPE} = \\frac{100\\%}{n} \\sum \\left| \\frac{y_i - \\hat{y}_i}{y_i} \\right|$$
    """)
    render_explanation(
        "Mathematical Formulations & Statistical Methods",
        "This section documents the formal mathematical equations powering BananaScope PH's calculations. "
        "All growth, regression, anomaly detection, and exponential smoothing algorithms follow standard statistical methodologies."
    )
    render_view_footer("MATH_METHODOLOGY")


